"text": "The gates are the workspace lint pair, the harness `run` in its unit and default (integration + E2E, including the new `contract_` binary) selections, three targeted filters for this chunk's new tests, `cargo deny`, the local pre-push gate, and a harness smoke. - The smoke boots a session with step 4 in place and reads two things from the session's own logs: the stamp   (`cli_verified:true` on the wrapper's `claude-child` start line) and readiness line 3. A second boot with   `--unstamped` is read the same way. - The CLI refusal of `--local-live` under `CI` is asserted directly (v1-14). - The positive `--local-live` run drives the real `claude` on the operator's subscription (one Haiku turn), so it is NOT   a gate. The operator may run it once in the operator pass (`bash scripts/agent-run.sh run --unit --local-live`) and   record the document in `evidence/`. - The chunk's verdict is CI's on all three OSes (the per-OS `test` job, `gate --require coverage,doctest,playwright`),   read after the operator's push. - No measurement pushes (P4 fork)."
}
],
